Aegis
Copyright (c) 2026 skunkworks

This product is original work. It is a clean-room reimplementation: its design
is informed by reading two open-source security-analysis frameworks, but it
contains no code copied, pasted, or vendored from them. Each subsystem is
specified in our own words under docs/specs/ and implemented from that spec.

Derived patterns are credited below. Credit here acknowledges influence on
architecture and behavior; it does not imply any shared source code.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Strix — https://github.com/usestrix/strix (Apache-2.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Patterns whose *shape* informed Aegis:
  * Graph-of-agents multi-agent orchestration (dynamic engine, M2).
  * Findings knowledge base with CVSS scoring and OWASP classification.
  * LLM-style deduplication of findings (same-underlying-vulnerability check).
  * True-positive triage before expensive write-up/PoC work.
  * SKILL.md / MCP-server extension points.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RAPTOR — https://github.com/gadievron/raptor (MIT)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Patterns whose *shape* informed Aegis:
  * Hypothesis-driven audit engine (evidence + coverage + posterior/verdict).
  * Staged /validate exploitability gate chain (short-circuiting).
  * Wrappers for Semgrep / CodeQL (+ SMT path-feasibility), SCA, binary
    analysis, fuzzing, crash analysis, dynamic instrumentation, web testing.
  * Specialist personas and a labeled regression corpus with calibration.
  * Per-run cost caps and a credential-holding dispatcher; a mechanical
    --no-llm mode.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Jev / TypeSafe AI — typed "System One" decision model
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The typed-decision concept (choose / score / boolean with a probability)
informed the aegis.decision layer's interface. Aegis depends on no vendor:
JevBackend is one optional backend among several, and Aegis runs fully offline
with StaticBackend or against a localhost model server with BasalOmniBackend.
